The World provides all the basic ECS functionality of Larecs through it’s member storage. These include functions like HostStorage.query, HostStorage.add_entity, HostStorage.add, HostStorage.remove, HostStorage.get or HostStorage.remove_entity.

data.run-the-kernel-from-a-system#Run the ker:
A system holds application logic and runs once per simulation step. Move runs the kernel:
@fieldwise_init struct Move(System): """Runs the `move` kernel once per step.""" def update(mut self, mut context: SystemContext[...]) raises: """Moves all particles. Args: context: Access to the scheduler's world. Raises: Error: If `Time` is missing from the world. """ context.run[move]() Move implements the System trait. The scheduler calls its update method once per step and passes a SystemContext. SystemContext[...] lets the compiler infer the context’s parameters from the world it belongs to. context.run[move]() calls move for the particles that match move_filter.
System also offers initialize and finalize, which run once before the first and after the last step. Move keeps their default empty implementations.
